# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DVC-tracked data (see .dvc/config, `make data-pull`)
#
# These three paths hold real vendor/commenter data or regenerable pipeline
# output. They are versioned in DVC and stored in Cloudflare R2, NOT in git -
# each one has a committed *.dvc pointer file recording its content hash, so
# every git commit pins the exact data it was produced against.
#
# The actual ignore rules are written by DVC itself into scoped .gitignore
# files next to each path (data/.gitignore, and the entries at the bottom of
# this file) - don't duplicate them here.
#
#   runs/            raw Graph API dumps, catalogs, profiles, OCR cache. Since
#                    the Meta app went Live (2026-10-17) these carry real
#                    commenters' text.
#   data/snapshots/  Stage 6 baselines incl. caption embeddings
#   report/          harness predictions + token logs (the evidence behind
#                    every figure)
#
# eval/golden/ is committed to git, not DVC (see CLAUDE.md).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets - includes .dvc/config.local (R2 credentials), ignored by .dvc/.gitignore
.env
*.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# The Ubuntu (WSL) side's environment, kept apart from Windows' .venv/ via
# UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT - see CLAUDE.md.
.venv-linux/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

.vscode/

# Scratch/working files - local only
scratch_*.txt
scratch_*.json
*.bak

# --- written by `dvc add` ---
/report

# Sponsor's internal brief - local reference only, never committed.
# The README's "What the brief asked for" section is the public stand-in.
poc/
/runs
